An Azure governance operating model defines how people, processes, and technologies work together to manage cloud resources responsibly.

The model can define:

* Governance responsibilities
* Policy ownership
* Security responsibilities
* Subscription administration
* Cost management
* Compliance processes
* Exception handling
* Operational reviews

For example, a central cloud governance team may define organization-wide policies while individual application teams remain responsible for their workloads.

A real-life use case is a large enterprise establishing a Cloud Center of Excellence that coordinates security, finance, infrastructure, and application teams.

A governance operating model creates clear accountability without unnecessarily preventing application teams from working independently.
